I looked at all 14 crops before opening `review.json`. Most of the readings you gave me hold up, but one does not.

**Main disagreement: haft-instruction.** The crop reads **המפטיר יברך ברכות אחרונות.** with no ה. In this rabbinic type, the first letter of אחרונות is the same glyph that starts אומר in the shemu-parenthesis crop, which is an alef. The ה at the start of המפטיר and הש״ץ is a different glyph, and none appears before אחרונות. So the first review was right and its fix should be applied. Your note that the crop "clearly" has ה is the reading I'd treat as the false correction.

**Two readings I couldn't settle at this resolution:** whether ט in בטחנו has a meteg, and whether ב in בחסד has a meteg. The native-resolution crops were also too small for me to rule out a dagesh in the ת of בתינו. I listed these as unresolved rather than confirming or rejecting them.

